$Aeon::Books["xBinding","title"] = "Key Binding";
$Aeon::Books["xBinding","rntTm"] = "3600";
$Aeon::Books["xBinding","feeRn"] = "0";
$Aeon::Books["xBinding","feeLt"] = "10";
$Aeon::Books["xBinding","feeRp"] = "200";
$Aeon::Books["xBinding","cntnt"] = "<f2>Key Binding<f1> is a very powerful tool unique to the Aeon world, using it you can simplify in-game commands without the use of external scripts! By pressing your '<f2>Beacon Key<f1>' you can open up your <f3>Key Binding Menu<f1>, then select a key, then select what to assign that key to! It is very simple and easy to use, but is often overlooked. You can assign keys to do many things, including: <f2>Chat <f2>Commands<f1>, <f2>Construction <f2>Tool <f2>Options<f1>, <f2>Skill Options<f1>, <f2>Trade<f1>, <f2>Interact<f1>, and even set <f2>Presets<f1> for all of the keys! <f3>Chat Command<f1> binding allows you to bind a key to call a Chat Command such as '<f2>#save<f1>' and '<f2>#grab<f1>', so you don't have to type them every time! <f3>Construction Tool Options<f1> allow you to set a key to switch the CnTool Mode to whichever mode you select! <f3>Skill Options<f1> binding allows you to bind a key to perform any <f2>Skill Funcs<f1> that are available to you, or open the <f2>Skills Menu<f1>! <f3>Trade<f1> is a pretty self explanitory binding, however seldom used it may be. <f3>Interact<f1> binding is crucial, by default the '<f2>Grenade Key<f1>' is set to perform Interaction, which is used to activate Doors, Terminals, Teleporters, and other miscellaneous operations throughout Aeon! Finally you can set <f3>Presets<f1> for all of the keys, such as the '<f2>Construction Preset<f1>' which assigns all the keys to CnTool Modes! In conclusion, Key Binding is a very important and useful aspect of Aeon, so learn to love it!";